{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-399",
  "title": "Project Viability",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Project Viability"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Q"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "# 1. Raster.tv"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What it is**: A modern, cloud‑hosted platform for community and public‑access TV stations to manage programming, member submissions, and streaming across web, mobile, and OTT in one place."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What problem it solves**: Replaces fragmented, outdated workflows (Cablecast backends, manual submission portals, ad‑hoc captioning, scattered links) with a unified system that reduces admin time, improves accessibility, and makes content discovery effortless."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Who needs it**: Station managers and programming coordinators at community media centers and municipal TV channels, plus membership/community coordinators responsible for creator onboarding and compliance."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What you've built**: A working beta with core station hub, member submission flow, early Cablecast and Nexudus integration points, AI captioning pipeline exploration, and a Framer/Nuxt front end deployed to staging for partner feedback."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Why now**: Stations face cord‑cutting, accessibility and compliance pressure, aging infrastructure, and new funding windows; modern tools and AI captioning make it feasible to upgrade workflows and audience reach today."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "# 2. Amorphous"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What it is**: A local-first, AI-assisted spatial canvas that pulls files, links, and live web into zoomable boards."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Problem it solves**: Creative reference sprawl and sluggish browser boards; arranging thousands of assets by hand; brittle embeds; offline gaps."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Who needs it**: Art directors, illustrators, concept artists (primary). PMs/researchers are secondary—not your wedge."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What you’ve built**: Solid core: layers/depth, culling, drag-drop, file explorer, node types, webview shim, Tauri shell. Missing wedge-makers: native webviews, directory watchers, global quick-capture, export/share, hardened CSP/creds."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Why now**: Tauri 2 is stable, on-device embeddings are cheap, and Milanote/Miro hit browser ceilings. Offline/local-first is back in fashion."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "# 3. Pocketflow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What it is:** Opinionated ecommerce ops hub that plugs **Webflow + Stripe + Shippo** to handle inventory, labels, tracking write-backs, and digital delivery."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Problem it solves:** Merchants duct-taping zaps and manual Shippo steps; no single source of truth or reliable tracking back to Webflow (other forntend providers coming soon)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Who needs it:** Small, single-warehouse Webflow stores that want a 10-minute setup, not plugins + scripts."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What you’ve built:** Clear PB data model, Hono API/webhooks, admin UI scaffold, job runners; a 4-week v0 plan (read-only) with definition of done and client E2E checklist."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Why now:** Webflow stores are growing but under-tooled; your opinionated stack replaces fragile automations. (Your own kill-rules + pricing show clarity on execution risk.)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "# 4. Nodebook"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What it is:** Agent-native, local-first workspace that unifies email, calendar, notes, and tasks into a programmable graph for persistent, context-aware agents."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Problem it solves:** “Goldfish memory” + copy-paste hell across tools; AI assistants don’t retain/act on long-term personal context."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Who needs it:** Solo operators/power users (founders, researchers, execs) already hacking Notion/Obsidian/ChatGPT and craving a real agentic OS."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What you’ve built:** Concept, pitch, market analysis, strategy; prototypes and integrations are described but traction is pre-product (founder-used, waitlist/comms plan)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Why now:** Shift to agent-native computing; incumbents tease it (e.g., Apple Intelligence) but don’t deliver persistent context—clear timing wedge."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "# 5. TurtleBase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What it is (one sentence):** A “virtual PocketBase” platform: multi-tenant PB + gateway + CLI that spins up **realtime pocket-sized DBs** for mini-apps, with schema diff/typegen and admin tooling."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What problem it solves (specific pain):** Shipping many tiny apps on PocketBase is brittle—tenancy, schema migrations, type safety, and realtime coordination are ad-hoc; TurtleBase standardizes **app scoping, schema/rules, and live updates** so you stop rebuilding glue each time."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Who needs it (specific persona):** **Agency tech lead** (or indie founder-engineer) managing multiple client minis/services who wants safe multi-tenant PB, quick schema iteration, and a unified admin/runbook."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What you’ve built (how far along):** Clear architecture + gateway (Hono/Next runtime), core package (schema diff, migrations, PB wrappers, typegen, realtime), admin CLI, collections layout; recent fixes on ports/headers and members schema. Status: **Development Phase**—no public GA yet."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Why now (timing/catalyst):** PB is surging for MVPs, teams need faster multi-tenant scaffolding; parallel trend toward **local-first/offline** (your “TurtleDB” vision) strengthens the wedge if/when you push client-side runtime later."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "# 6. CursiveCode"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What it is (one sentence):** A VS Code extension that lets you compose programs visually (node/edge graphs) and generates executable TypeScript/JavaScript from the flow."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What problem it solves (specific pain):** Rapid prototyping and teaching complex data/logic flows is slow and error-prone in pure text; teams reinvent boilerplate, struggle to “see” control/data flow, and can’t easily reuse/share patterns."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Who needs it (specific person/role):** A **staff-level front-end/platform engineer** who prototypes data transforms and UI logic in VS Code and must hand off reusable patterns to less code-heavy teammates (design technologists, QA, educators)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **What you’ve built (how far along):** Working prototype: custom editor for `.cursive`, ReactFlow canvas, basic node types, library system (`.cursivelib`), theme sync, commands, and baseline TS/JS codegen with example files."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Why now (timing/catalyst):** VS Code has become the universal IDE; ReactFlow and webview APIs are mature; growing appetite for visual/AI-assisted authoring (Node-RED/Blueprints wave) and for artifacts that both **explain and execute**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-41",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-40",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Okay, let me hit each one with YC scoring and brutal honesty.**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-44",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "## 1. Raster.tv"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-45",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**YC Viability: 3/10**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Biggest Strength:** Clear, underserved niche with real budget (public access TV stations have funding)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-47",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Fatal Flaw:** Tiny market. There are ~3,000 public access stations in the US. Even if you capture 50%, that's $1.5M ARR at $1K/month—not a $1B outcome."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**What it would take:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-49",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Pivot to broader \"community video platforms\"** (churches, schools, local governments)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-50",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Show that public access is just the wedge into a $10B+ market"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Get 50+ stations signed up (prove you can capture the niche fast)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-52",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**YC's concern:** \"This is a nice business, but is it venture-scale?\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-53",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**My take:** This is a **great lifestyle business** ($500K-$2M ARR), not a YC company. Unless you can show it's a Trojan horse into a much bigger market."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-54",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-55",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "## 2. Amorphous"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-56",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**YC Viability: 6/10**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-57",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Biggest Strength:** Clear wedge (art directors), timely (Tauri 2, local-first hype), and you're building for a real workflow pain."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-58",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Fatal Flaw:** Competitive moat is unclear. What stops Miro/Milanote from adding offline mode? What stops Figma from adding this?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-59",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**What it would take:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-60",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Get 100 paying art directors using it** (prove willingness to pay)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-61",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Show **10x better performance** for large canvases (technical moat)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-62",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Demonstrate **network effects** (shared asset libraries? template marketplace?)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-63",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**YC's concern:** \"Cool tool, but is this a feature or a platform?\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-64",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**My take:** This is **borderline**. If you can show strong early adoption + clear moat (e.g., \"only tool that handles 10K+ assets smoothly\"), it's fundable. But you need **traction proof** before applying."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-65",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-66",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "## 3. Pocketflow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-67",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**YC Viability: 5/10**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-68",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Biggest Strength:** Clear pain (Webflow ecommerce ops are janky), paying customers exist, you've scoped MVP well."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-69",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Fatal Flaw:** Small TAM and commoditizing fast. How many Webflow stores are there? And once Webflow itself adds this, you're done."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-70",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**What it would take:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-71",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **10+ paying customers at $100+/month** before applying"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-72",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Expand beyond Webflow (Shopify? Wix? Make it platform-agnostic)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-73",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Show you're building **infrastructure**, not a Webflow plugin"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-74",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**YC's concern:** \"This is a nice Webflow plugin. Why won't Webflow just build this themselves?\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-75",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**My take:** **Bootstrap this, don't VC-fund it.** Get to $50K MRR, then maybe apply to YC as \"ecommerce ops infrastructure\" (broader positioning)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-76",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-77",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "## 4. Nodebook"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-78",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**YC Viability: 7/10**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-79",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Biggest Strength:** PERFECT TIMING. Agent-native computing is the hottest thing in AI right now. YC is funding multiple agent startups per batch."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-80",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Fatal Flaw:** No product yet. YC funds ideas, but you need SOMETHING working—even if it's hacky."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-81",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**What it would take:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-82",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Build a working prototype in 2 weeks** (ugly is fine)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-83",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Use it yourself daily** for 30 days (dogfooding is critical)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-84",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Get **10 people in your network using it** (waitlist doesn't count)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-85",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Frame as **\"the operating system for AI agents\"** (infrastructure play)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-86",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**YC's concern:** \"Love the vision, but do you have anything working?\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-87",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**My take:** **This is your best YC shot**, but you need to ship FAST. Build the ugliest possible MVP that works for YOU, then apply. This market is hot RIGHT NOW—don't wait 6 months."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-88",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-89",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "## 5. TurtleBase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-90",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**YC Viability: 4/10**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-91",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Biggest Strength:** Clear technical execution, real problem (multi-tenant PocketBase is painful)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-92",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Fatal Flaw:** Developer infrastructure is a HARD sell. Your market is \"people who already chose PocketBase\" (niche within a niche)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-93",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**What it would take:**"
